{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778518098,"nonce":"3SjeL9X33az2IUCIT9ur7UanWYU=","title":"Design: project-config-driven figure routing via package registry","message":"Tracks the implementation of feedbax-side figure-save routing for application packages. Captures design rationale; the actual code lands as the implementation of this issue.\n\n## Background\n\nApplication packages (e.g., rlrmp) need to save figures to a dual-tree layout: light spec to a tracked `results/.../figures/\u003ctopic\u003e/` and heavy render to a gitignored `_artifacts/.../figures/\u003ctopic\u003e/`, with a symlink in the spec dir for unified local navigation. Today each caller does this manually (`save_figure_with_spec` writes spec + render to one dir; the caller maintains both paths). Friction: every save site duplicates routing logic.\n\n## Decision\n\n**Single feedbax API parameterized by package + experiment + topic; project config drives routing.**\n\nAPI (new):\n```python\nfeedbax.plot.save_figure(fig, spec, *, package, experiment, topic)\n```\n\nLooks up `package` in the existing `EXPERIMENT_REGISTRY`, reads its `figure_routing` config, resolves both paths from templates, writes spec to spec_dir, render to render_dir, creates a relative symlink if configured. **One API; no separate `save_figure_dual_tree` variant.**\n\nRouting config lives in `register_package_from_module_info(..., figure_routing={...})` for the first iteration. Schema:\n```python\nfigure_routing = {\n    \"spec_dir_template\": \"results/{experiment}/figures/{topic}\",\n    \"render_dir_template\": \"_artifacts/{experiment}/figures/{topic}\",\n    \"spec_format\": \"json\",\n    \"render_format\": \"html\",\n    \"create_symlink_in_spec_dir\": True,\n}\n```\n\n## Rationale\n\n- **Single API**: routing variants live in config, not in function names. Avoids `save_figure`, `save_figure_dual_tree`, `save_figure_with_symlink`, etc. — combinatorial explosion as conventions grow.\n- **Project config, not feedbax config**: feedbax stays generic; each application package declares its own layout. Other feedbax applications can adopt different layouts without affecting each other.\n- **Registry as the routing source**: leverages the just-fixed entry-point system (`efb99b8`); no new mechanism to maintain.\n- **Templates with `{experiment}`/`{topic}` substitution**: declarative, agent-readable, supports future variations (e.g., flat-by-hash layout will just change the template strings).\n\n## Editable-install assumption + defensive guard\n\nApplication packages (rlrmp et al.) are research scaffolding — editable-installed in a development checkout, NOT pip-installed library packages. `__file__` of the registered package module must resolve to the checkout root for `results/` and `_artifacts/` to be writable in the right place. If the package were pip-installed to site-packages, writes would land in site-packages — bad.\n\n**Cheap insurance**: a guard in the routing helper that checks the package module is in an editable install (presence of `.git` near `__file__`) and warns or errors otherwise. Implementation: walk parents of `__file__` looking for `.git`; warn if not found within N levels. No false positives in practice.\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- `efb99b8` — prereq: entry-point discovery fix (merged via auth `814d73fa`).\n- `5f22fa7` — future: migrate routing config from `register_*` kwargs to `[tool.feedbax]` in pyproject.toml.\n- `bdee8d1` — docs: integration pattern (research-app pattern + editable install + figure routing).\n- rlrmp `0f1af24` — surfacing context: symlink mirror-tree on the rlrmp side.\n- rlrmp `f485c26` — surfacing context: results/ hierarchy reorganization (flat-by-hash).\n\n## Implementation scope (this issue)\n\n- Extend `register_package_from_module_info` with `figure_routing` kwarg + storage in `ExperimentRegistry`.\n- Implement `feedbax.plot.save_figure(fig, spec, *, package, experiment, topic)`.\n- Implement editable-install guard.\n- Add preliminary docs to feedbax README under \"Building application packages on feedbax\".\n- Do NOT migrate rlrmp call sites here — that lives in the rlrmp-side reorg work.","files":null}]}